## The Near Arch

::bg{location="tollbridge" time="dusk"}
::music{action="change" mood="sad" volume="down"}
@narrator: The chain is down because someone cut it. Crossbows lie along the parapet like dropped cutlery. The gorge takes the smoke and gives back nothing.
@narrator{when="holds('fell', ['maelis'])"}: Maelis of Coldwater lies across the chain she guarded. Somebody has closed her eyes. Nobody will say who.
@narrator{when="!holds('fell', ['maelis'])"}: Maelis is not among the dead. Her people say she went over the parapet on a rope when the chain fell, and that she will be back.
@corvin{when="holds('inParty', ['corvin'])"}: Well. That's one way to pay a toll.
@isolde{when="holds('inParty', ['isolde']) && holds('fell', ['maelis'])"}: I knew her brother. Now I have known them both.
@wren{when="@wrenWithUs"}: The river's loud tonight. It's angry. It has a right to be.
@narrator{when="occasion.payload.wagonsLost >= 1"}: The Company's count comes to {{occasion.payload.wagonsLost:plural(one wagon|#word wagons)}} fewer than it was this morning.
::set{run.wagons -= occasion.payload.wagonsLost}
::set{run.rep.dusk -= 2}
::set{run.rep.company += 1}
